      ],
      "orig": "In general, an electric vehicle is designed in such a way that motors are rotated using a battery 40 as a power source to drive the wheels, thereby to make the vehicle travel. There is a type of electric vehicle in which a left wheel and a right wheel are driven by individual motors. When the left wheel and the right wheel are driven by individual motors 20, 22, it is possible to control the motors independently of each other so as to improve steering. However, when an abnormality occurs in the rotation of one motor, the vehicle may get into a state in which it is difficult to control, especially at high speed; in the most serious case, the vehicle spins. It is therefore a principal object of the present invention to provide an electric vehicle which is capable of travelling properly even when an abnormality occurs in the rotation of one of the left-wheel motor 20 or the right-wheel motor 22. The controller 30 for an electric vehicle is constructed by three or more microprocessors to monitor a run away state of the microprocessors mutually, so that a motor is not accelerated or decelerated abnormally if one microprocessor fails.",
      "text": "In general, an electric vehicle is designed in such a way that motors are rotated using a battery 40 as a power source to drive the wheels, thereby to make the vehicle travel. There is a type of electric vehicle in which a left wheel and a right wheel are driven by individual motors. When the left wheel and the right wheel are driven by individual motors 20, 22, it is possible to control the motors independently of each other so as to improve steering. However, when an abnormality occurs in the rotation of one motor, the vehicle may get into a state in which it is difficult to control, especially at high speed; in the most serious case, the vehicle spins. It is therefore a principal object of the present invention to provide an electric vehicle which is capable of travelling properly even when an abnormality occurs in the rotation of one of the left-wheel motor 20 or the right-wheel motor 22. The controller 30 for an electric vehicle is constructed by three or more microprocessors to monitor a run away state of the microprocessors mutually, so that a motor is not accelerated or decelerated abnormally if one microprocessor fails."
    },
